3 facts and a country
- This is one of the 3 most western countries in Europe.  It has the northern most capital city in the world. It is smaller than Florida (Iceland - Actually the most western euro country if you exclude the Azores islands)
- 6th Largest population. Flag contains 3 of the 5 Olympic colors. Borders 10 other countries. (Brazil)
- It is one of only two completely landlocked countries on its continent. It has two capital cities. It holds roughly 50% to 70% of the world's known lithium reserves, mostly located beneath massive salt flats. (Bolivia - The other landlocked country in South America is Paraguay)
- This country has a square national flag.  It has four official languages, none of which are English. It has enough fortified nuclear fallout shelters to accommodate over 100% of its national population. (Switzerland)
- It is one of only three sovereign countries in the world that are completely surrounded by a single other country aka Enclave.  Its national flag is majority yellow and white.  It uses the Euro as its official currency (Vatican City - Other enclaves are San Marino [also surrounded by Italy] and Lesotho, surrounded by South Africa)
- It is an island nation situated in the Indian Ocean. It is the world's leading producer of vanilla, historically supplying roughly 80% of the global market. English is not one of their official languages (Madagascar - Official langagues are Malagasy and French.  Indonesia also fits these hints, [Official language Bahasa Indonesia] xcept they are the second largest producer of Vanilla [20-25% of global supply])
- This country is one of only three surviving, fully sovereign city-states in the modern world.  This country has one of the highest GDP per capita.  Its territory is located just one degree north of the equator.
- This country lies on the Mediterranean Sea.  Halloumi cheese originated exclusively here.  This country was a major source of copper (Cyprus)
- As of 2023 it is the most populated country in the world.  It is home to the tallest statue in the world, standing at 182 meters - nearly double the height of the Statue of Liberty.  It is one of the top 3 tea producers in the world (India - China is the number 1 tea producer, India is #2)
- It has the longest continuous coastline of any country on its continent.  It houses a "Doomsday Vault" designed to safely store backups of the world's crop seeds.  Its flag boasts a cross. (Norway)

